From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] identify_os: recognise native riscv64 hosts

lnxriscv64 is a supported PLAT, but dev/make/identify_os.sh only maps
uname -m x86_64 and aarch64, so on a native riscv64 host it prints
"Unknown architecture: riscv64". Upstream only builds riscv64 by
cross-compiling from an x86_64 host, so this is never hit there.

On a native riscv64 build with PLAT=lnxriscv64, every make release
target (daal, onedal_c) depends on _release_common -> _release_nuspec,
which runs deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh. That script feeds the
multi-word identify_os.sh output unquoted to [ ], then falls through to
"Unknown platform Unknown architecture: riscv64" and exits 1, failing
the build before anything is compiled.

Print lnxriscv64 for riscv64 and give prepare_dal_nuget.sh a matching
branch (platform linux, libs under lib/riscv64, the release layout the
makefile produces for this PLAT). As a side effect the makefile now sees
PLAT == IDENTIFIED_PLAT and stops treating the native build as a cross
build, so clang no longer gets --target=riscv64-linux-gnu, matching how
a native lnxarm build is handled.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [native riscv64 build support; upstream CI only cross-compiles riscv64 from x86_64]
---
 deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh | 7 +++++++
 dev/make/identify_os.sh           | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh b/deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh
index 5d115c7..adf007c 100755
--- a/deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh
+++ b/deploy/nuget/prepare_dal_nuget.sh
@@ -67,6 +67,13 @@ create_package() {
         dynamic_lib_path=lib/arm
         static_lib_path=lib/arm
         lib_prefix=libonedal
+    elif [ ${platform} = "lnxriscv64" ]; then
+        platform=linux
+        tbb_platform=linux
+        rls_prefix=${rls_dir}/daal/latest
+        dynamic_lib_path=lib/riscv64
+        static_lib_path=lib/riscv64
+        lib_prefix=libonedal

     elif [ ${platform} = "mac32e" ]; then
         platform=osx-x64
diff --git a/dev/make/identify_os.sh b/dev/make/identify_os.sh
index 2a45ecc..d26ac8c 100755
--- a/dev/make/identify_os.sh
+++ b/dev/make/identify_os.sh
@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@ if [ "${os}" = "Linux" ]; then
     echo lnx32e
   elif [ "${ARCH}" = "aarch64" ]; then
     echo lnxarm
+  elif [ "${ARCH}" = "riscv64" ]; then
+    echo lnxriscv64
   else
     echo "Unknown architecture: ${ARCH}"
     exit 1
--
